{"id": "EUVD-2026-96991", "enisaUuid": "b18e3c51-03a2-3068-a77a-cdd984d9ed2b", "description": "Combodo iTop 3.1.0 through 3.3.0 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in LinkSetController.php that allows authenticated console users to bypass profile grants by supplying arbitrary class and key parameters. Attackers can invoke the linkset delete, detach and get-remote-object routes to delete objects, clear external keys, and read object attributes without permission.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T12:19:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:50:02", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind03/itop-linkset-unchecked-delete-detach-read-20261011", "https://github.com/Combodo/iTop/blob/3.3.0/sources/Controller/Links/LinkSetController.php#L43-L121", "https://github.com/Combodo/iTop/blob/3.3.0/sources/Controller/Links/LinkSetController.php#L272-L301", "https://github.com/Combodo/iTop", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/combodo-itop-3.1.0-through-3.3.0-missing-authorization-via-linksetcontroller"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108717", "GHSA-p2cr-76v5-5835"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "46fad152-7386-3895-bd63-7b445c7779e6", "product": {"name": "iTop", "vendor": {"name": "Combodo"}}, "product_version": "3.1.0 \u22643.3.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6f7e928a-72e8-3350-bc9f-e343d60de2fc", "vendor": {"name": "Combodo"}}], "isExploited": false}